## Context
Author decision (2026-11-09): the design-history directory `conception/` is renamed
`design/`, harness first, then every project (alignment tickets filed in each project
the same day). Reasons given: `conception` misleads English readers and models; `design/`
is the conventional name; `notes/` was rejected (vague, collides with `refs/notes/review`).
A sweep of padme and doudou the same day found no project ignoring `conception/`; the
residue is research projects still tracking design material under `docs/`, which is
meant to be git-ignored staging.

Scale on origin/main 2026-11-09: 312 tracked files under `conception/`; live references
in scripts (21 files), skills (19), tests (16), projects/ (16), memory topics, adapters
(4), rules (3), hooks (1), README/STATE/ROADMAP/AGENTS.md, `.gitignore` (`!conception/`).

## Decisions for the Imagine phase
- History stays as written: `tickets/closed/`, `memory/journal/`, review records and
  commit messages keep `conception/` paths. Decide whether a short `conception/README.md`
  redirect (or a symlink) is kept for old links, and for how long.
- Open tickets, memory topics, rules, skills, scripts, tests, docstrings and the
  `.gitignore` allowlist move to `design/`.
- `projects/` registry entries and any per-project template or installer step that
  names `conception/` change in the same PR, so new projects start on `design/`.
- `rules/workflow.md` names `conception/design-note-template.md`; skills such as raid,
  hunt, roar's attribution contract and route cite memos by path.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `git mv conception design` with history-preserving renames; no file content lost
      (byte-compare the tree before and after, paths aside)
- [ ] `git grep -n 'conception/'` outside the history set above returns nothing, or each
      remaining hit is listed in the PR as deliberate
- [ ] `make check` passes
- [ ] The cross-project alignment tickets cite this ticket and can start once it lands

## Imagine (raid 632b19, 2026-11-09)
Shape: one PR, two commits. (a) `git mv conception design` plus the `.gitignore` allowlist
swap (`!conception/` → `!design/`); renames only, so `-M100%` and `--follow` hold; red on
its own and says so. (b) one path-scoped reference sweep (rules/workflow.md rename rule).
No redirect README, no symlink: no runtime consumer found, and both would pollute the
exit-criterion grep. Playbook: `memory/journal/2026/2026-10-27-docs-to-conception-pr1744.md`
(the docs/→conception/ move): rewrite by exact name, restore hash-pinned records byte-identical.

Runtime paths that break silently if missed: `.gitignore:37-38`, `scripts/census/deps.py:28`,
`scripts/trace_ab_harvest.py:223-224` (+ skills/trace-doctor/SKILL.md), `scripts/check-personal-data.sh:6,10`,
`scripts/local-ci-negative-controls.sh:59`, `memory/MEMORY.md:4-5` (live link into memory-v8).
Link-mapping tests: `tests/test_memory_v8_pilot.py:70` and `tests/test_dream_v8.py:182` map
docs/X→conception/X; they must now send docs/X and conception/X → design/X so frozen journal
and evidence links (15 relative links under memory/) stay as written and the relocation test
stays green. `tests/test_retired_skill_names.py:5` exemption → design/.

Frozen, left as written: tickets/closed, memory/journal, memory/smelts, memory/evidence
(attribution anchors like `conception/README.md:3`), projects/* (ticket 1480's territory),
commit messages, dated memos inside the moved tree, the French word (tests/test_gaze_prose_routing.py),
`memory/.provenance.json` slug, tests/fixtures (sha256-pinned), and `adapters/codex/hooks.json:2`
(the description string is part of the trusted hook definition; listed as a deliberate remainder).

Transitional wording, both directions since some projects (padme 0111) aligned first:
`rules/prose-adherence-tests.md:5,18`, `rules/README.md:32`, `skills/gaze/references/prose-panel.md:22-23`
name `design/editorial-brief.md`, falling back to `conception/` until the alignment tickets close.
The "projects/ registry entries" decision is vacuous: no registry or installer template names the
harness conception/; the PR says so.

Byte-compare: `diff <(git ls-tree -r BASE:conception) <(git ls-tree -r A:design)` empty, and
`git diff --summary -M100% BASE A` shows 312 renames and nothing else (plumbing, not rtk counts).
Generated: `make skills-catalog` expected no-op, then `make check-skills-drift`; `python3 -m json.tool`
on edited adapters/*.json.

Later review: at the next molt sweep ~2026-11-23 or when the alignment tickets close, rerun the
sweep across projects; then drop the transitional `conception/` fallback with a log line here.
Blind-Spot pass: 3 material findings (playbook, link-mapping chain, pinned files), folded above.

## Plan
Actions, in the hunt worktree:
1. Commit (a): `git mv conception design`; swap the two `.gitignore` lines; run the byte-compare.
2. Commit (b): sweep `conception/` → `design/` on the live pathspec only
   (`':!tickets/closed' ':!memory/journal' ':!memory/smelts' ':!memory/evidence' ':!projects' ':!tests/fixtures' ':!adapters/codex/hooks.json' ':!memory/.provenance.json'`,
   slash-terminated pattern, French word excluded), review the diff for `design/design`
   and relative-link depth; chain the two test mappings; retitle the two prose-panel spots
   with the fallback wording; fix relative links inside design/ live docs (README, template, index).
3. First test (red before step 2, green after): `uv run pytest tests/test_memory_v8_pilot.py tests/test_dream_v8.py -m integration`
   fails on the journal links after commit (a) alone (positive control), passes after the mapping chain.
4. `make check`; `scripts/local-ci-negative-controls.sh`; the remainder grep pasted in the PR as deliberate.
Dependencies: none. Ticket 1480 stays separate.

## Feasibility
